{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>But if they do not cross over armed with you.</b> The meaning is: even though they may cross over afterward, they shall be absorbed among you. And the reason he said <b>וְנֹאחֲזוּ</b> with the addition of a vav, and did not say ״יֵאָחֲזוּ״, is to allude to the inference that their success is heard from the phrase ״אִם יַעַבְרוּ״ in this manner — and if they do not cross over, they will not succeed in that land, and of their own accord they shall be absorbed among you because of the constriction they experience in the land, and it turns out that they have nullified the commandment and what is theirs has not reached them."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:55.424442891Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}